  <title id="bdl27fsmolresults-title">Mean performance of each compared method on the FS-Mol test tasks</title>
  <desc id="bdl27fsmolresults-desc">Two line plots against support set size 16, 32, 64, 128 and 256. Left, classification on 157 tasks, change in AUPRC: ADKF-IFT is highest at every size, rising from about 0.23 to about 0.33, followed by DKT and ProtoNet; CNP and GNN-MAML stay near 0.19; GP-ST, RF and GNN-MT rise from about 0.10 to about 0.25; kNN, PAR, DKL and MAT lie lower, and GNN-ST is lowest, near 0.02 to 0.06. Right, regression on 111 tasks, R squared out of sample: ADKF-IFT rises from about 0.17 to about 0.46 and DKT from about 0.17 to about 0.43; GP-ST and RF reach about 0.3; GNN-MT rises from about minus 0.06 to about 0.21; CNP, DKL and MAT stay low, MAT starting near minus 0.16.</desc>
